    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule: when `POST /api/owners` omits `registrationDate`, it defaults to the server's current date, and the value round-trips as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string.\n\nChanges (kept small and cohesive to minimize structural impact):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This flows into the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response, via `allOf`) as a `LocalDate`, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions \u2014 no mapper edit needed.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` field + accessors and `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`, plus the `LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (a 1-method class with zero surrounding complexity) \u2014 defaults the date to `LocalDate.now()` only when the mapped entity has none, leaving a supplied date untouched.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column and updated the positional seed INSERTs. Only the hsqldb scripts were touched, since they're the only ones kept in sync with the entity (the h2/mysql/postgres schemas already lack even the `email` column) and are what the tests use.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass and the full suite is green.",
